1
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:05,630
Hey, how are things going with your parents?

2
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:08,100
Not great. They hired divorce attorneys.

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,060
You know, speaking of attorneys,

4
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,540
if I ever needed a lawyer,

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:16,960
I would not hire She-Hulk.

6
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:18,960
You know what? That was almost on topic.

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,320
I'm gonna say, "Good job, Sheldon."

8
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,950
Wait, She-Hulk's a lawyer?

9
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,940
Yeah, she works at a law firm in New York.

10
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,360
Yes, but she's the only monster at the firm.

11
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,190
Between you, me and the wall,

12
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:35,550
I think she's an affirmative action hire.

13
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,550
Anyway, Dad's gonna be here in town,

14
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:40,150
so I won't be able to do Christmas dinner this year.

15
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,340
If you're not up to hosting Christmas dinner,

16
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,450
I'm happy to do it.

17
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,400
You can even bring your father.

18
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,800
That would be nice.

19
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,770
I've always wanted to do a traditional Victorian Christmas.

20
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:53,940
Parlor games, goose and figgy pudding...

21
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:56,780
English pudding.

22
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:58,680
Y-You get yourself all excited for pudding,

23
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:01,890
and here comes a cake with raisins in it.

24
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:03,510
I'm not going.

25
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:04,650
You're going.

26
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:06,690
Why do you hate me?

27
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,340
I don't hate you.

28
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:09,380
I love you.

29
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,090
Well, you call it love,

30
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:13,670
but it has a lot of raisins in it.

31
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,790
Amy, good luck getting these guys excited

32
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:18,260
about a dinner with a theme.

33
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:22,100
I gave up when no one cared about my Tom Hanks-giving.

34
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,080
I think a Victorian Christmas sounds nice.

35
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,150
- I agree. - Me, too.

36
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:29,320
You guys suck!

37
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,640
You know the best part of working in the clean room?

38
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,920
No allergies.

39
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,110
Check it out.

40
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:07,750
Oh, that-that... that's a lot of oxygen.

41
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,800
We should get going to Amy's.

42
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,290
Can you believe there was a time

43
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:13,800
when we would have needed an array

44
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,820
of giant Cherenkov telescopes to detect cosmic particles?

45
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,820
And here we are building our own multi-wire detector

46
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:22,770
like a couple of badasses.

47
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:25,030
I know. If we were still single,

48
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:28,180
we'd be tripping over all that booty.

49
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:32,720
Ladies do love a man dressed like a kitchen garbage bag.

50
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,180
Oh, no.

51
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,050
How the hell did a pigeon get in here?

52
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:45,270
- You shut the loading doors, right? - I thought you did.

53
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:47,480
Do you know what a disaster this is?!

54
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,560
You mean 'cause this room isn't supposed to have dust in it,

55
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:52,530
and we just let in a flying crap machine?!

56
00:02:53,690 --> 00:02:55,350
What do we do? Should we call someone?

57
00:02:55,350 --> 00:02:58,090
And tell them that we compromised all the equipment?

58
00:02:58,090 --> 00:03:01,060
Let's just get it out of here before anyone knows.

59
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:02,230
Okay, how do we catch it?

60
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:04,410
Well, what if we turn off all the lights

61
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:06,780
except for one, and it'll come to it.

62
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:10,070
It's not a moth!

63
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:12,750
Don't yell at me.

64
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:15,220
You're not gonna get any good ideas out of me if you're yelling.

65
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,700
Okay, so if I remain calm,

66
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,940
I'll get more gems like, "Turn off the lights"?!

67
00:03:20,830 --> 00:03:21,780
Great, we're turning on each other.

68
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:24,420
That's just what the bird wants us to do!

69
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,190
So, Dr. Koothrappali, long flight?

70
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:31,610
- 20 hours. - Oh, that's rough.

71
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:32,750
Not at all.

72
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:35,740
Did you know that when you fly transcontinental without your wife,

73
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:38,440
you don't pray for the plane to crash?

74
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:43,370
Can you please talk about anything else?

75
00:03:43,370 --> 00:03:44,710
Forgive me.

76
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,200
How are you and Leonard?

77
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,890
Oh, great. Everything's good.

78
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:50,560
- I see you got engaged. - Yes, we did.

79
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,920
Let me tell you a story.

80
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:52,900
Dad!

81
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:55,370
Sorry.

82
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:58,280
I'm sure you won't grow to hate each other.

83
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,190
Hey, Leonard. What's up?

84
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:07,700
What? How did that happen?

85
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,640
Yeah, okay. I'll be there as soon as I can.

86
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:12,200
Sorry. I have to run to the university.

87
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,280
What's going on?

88
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,920
There's been a problem with our experiment.

89
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:18,470
A bird got into the clean room.

90
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:19,950
You want me to come?

91
00:04:19,950 --> 00:04:21,470
Uh, no. You had a long flight.

92
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:23,090
You stay here and relax.

93
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:25,420
"Relax." Easy for you to say.

94
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:28,370
Your mother isn't cleaning out your bank account.

95
00:04:28,370 --> 00:04:31,710
40 years, the woman never cleaned a thing.

96
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,590
You're just gonna leave him here?

97
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:36,360
- "Relax," He says. - Yup. Bye.

98
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:41,270
* Here comes Santa Claus, here comes Santa Claus *

99
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:43,750
* Right down Santa Claus Lane *

100
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:46,290
* Vixen and Blitzen and all his reindeer *

101
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:48,060
* Pulling on the reins... *

102
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,450
Yeah, I appreciate the ride...

103
00:04:49,450 --> 00:04:51,190
* Bells are ringing, children singing *

104
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:53,500
* All is merry and bright *

105
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:56,050
* So hang your stockings and say your prayers *

106
00:04:56,050 --> 00:04:58,030
'Cause Santa Claus is coming tonight...

107
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:01,760
Why'd you turn it off?

108
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,580
Because in the last ten minutes, Santa came to town,

109
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:05,660
kissed Mommy

110
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:08,080
and ran Grandma over with a reindeer.

111
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,620
I had a drunk uncle who did all those things.

112
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:13,050
Nobody sings songs about him.

113
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:16,560
Maybe you'd like it more if you thought of Santa as a superhero

114
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:19,150
and his power is bringing joy to children.

115
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:21,810
My uncle was accused of that, too.

116
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:24,800
It turned out to be legal in Oklahoma.

117
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,470
Okay, new subject.

118
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:28,900
Let's talk about presents.

119
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:30,530
What did you get Amy?

120
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,710
Oh, we're not exchanging gifts.

121
00:05:32,710 --> 00:05:35,420
Come on, Sheldon, you have to get her something.

122
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:36,740
Why should I?

123
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:38,740
She knows that I don't like Christmas,

124
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:41,630
and yet, every year, she forces me to celebrate it.

125
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:44,620
Not only am I going to this foolish dinner against my will.

126
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:47,050
At the Christmas tree lot, there was mistletoe,

127
00:05:47,050 --> 00:05:49,490
and she kissed me under it in public.

128
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:53,030
Like we were the stars of a Tijuana sex show.

129
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:56,600
She's just excited about the holidays.

130
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,610
Yes, and she's not taking my feelings into account at all.

131
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:03,160
Maybe it's time I teach her a lesson.

132
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,720
How?

133
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:08,420
It'd have to be something heinous,

134
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:12,090
something that makes her as miserable as she's making me.

135
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,590
Oh, I've got it.

136
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,060
This is good.

137
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:19,550
What?

138
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:22,380
I'm going to buy her a present.

139
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,870
Yeah, you're gonna have to walk me through that.

140
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:29,730
With gift-giving, there's an implied social contract.

141
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:31,620
If I show up tonight with a present,

142
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,150
and she doesn't have one for me,

143
00:06:33,150 --> 00:06:35,690
she'll feel terrible.

144
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:38,280
Then you're both sad?

145
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,330
Yes.

146
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,480
Maybe she'll feel so guilty,

147
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:44,570
she'll never make me celebrate the holidays again.

148
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:48,680
So your evil plot here is to buy your girlfriend a present?

149
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,150
That's right.

150
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:53,420
So stay on my good side, or I'll get you a little something, too.

151
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,790
Okay, here's the plan.

152
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:03,630
I'm gonna put the food in the bag,

153
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:07,060
and when he lands in the bag to eat it, we close it up.

154
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:08,970
A Slim Jim?

155
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:11,550
It's all I could find. It'll work.

156
00:07:11,550 --> 00:07:12,160
Sure.

157
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:14,910
If the pigeon's stoned or a trucker.

158
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:17,880
Okay, well, what's your plan?

159
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,040
I told you my plan.

160
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,020
Let's call Building Services and get help.

161
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:24,040
And admit that we contaminated the clean room?

162
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,910
No, admit that you contaminated the clean room.

163
00:07:26,910 --> 00:07:29,520
Why do you keep assuming it was me?

164
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,530
Because you do this kind of thing all the time,

165
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:33,370
and then you try to cover it up.

166
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:34,440
Like when?

167
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:37,560
What about when you flipped the Mars Rover,

168
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,080
or lost Koothrappali's dog,

169
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:41,740
or almost drove off with that baby?

170
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:45,410
Again, it looked like my car, and the baby didn't even cry

171
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:48,420
until his mother punched me with her keys.

172
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,930
Fine, put the Slim Jim in the garbage bag.

173
00:07:50,930 --> 00:07:53,260
Well, what if you said it without sounding so condescending?

174
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:55,080
I can try, but your plan has the words

175
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:57,840
"Garbage bag" and "Slim Jim" in it!

176
00:07:59,020 --> 00:07:59,970
Hey, what's going on?

177
00:07:59,970 --> 00:08:01,560
Genius here wants to catch a bird

178
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,970
with a garbage bag and a Slim Jim.

179
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,850
Should have put it in the bag first.

180
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:18,440
So, if you don't mind me asking,

181
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,400
do you think you might start dating again?

182
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,900
It's much too soon for that.

183
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,380
Why? Do you know someone?

184
00:08:25,010 --> 00:08:26,890
No, but if things don't work out with me and Leonard,

185
00:08:26,890 --> 00:08:28,460
I'll give you a call.

186
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,900
Wait. How much do you talk about Star Trek?

187
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:37,230
Okay, let's get this Victorian party started.

188
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:38,370
I've done some research

189
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:40,840
about some traditional parlor games we can play.

190
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,240
Like what?

191
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:46,230
Well, there's a fun one called Ball of Wool.

192
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,300
You take a ball of wool,

193
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:52,110
and you put it right in the center of the table.

194
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:54,310
Then people sit on opposite sides of the table

195
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:56,690
and try to blow the wool off.

196
00:08:59,610 --> 00:09:02,580
Sorry. She's taken, too.

197
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:06,340
You know what I think your problem is?

198
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,310
You're jealous

199
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:09,470
because you and I used to be best friends

200
00:09:09,470 --> 00:09:11,760
until Koothrappali came along.

201
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,110
And you found somebody you could push around?

202
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:16,510
- Stay out of this. - Okay.

203
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:19,880
You know, maybe I'm best friends with Raj

204
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,470
because he doesn't think he's smarter than me.

205
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:24,740
- Actually... - I said, stay out of it!

206
00:09:24,990 --> 00:09:27,320
N-No. No, Raj, go ahead, say what you were gonna say.

207
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,500
All I'm gonna say is

208
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,630
you guys need to stop this right now.

209
00:09:30,630 --> 00:09:33,300
It-It's bad enough that my parents are fighting,

210
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,280
now I have to hear the two of you?

211
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,060
And who cares who's smarter?

212
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:38,820
If it's Leonard or me or...

213
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:41,540
you know, it's Christmas, let's say it's Howard.

214
00:09:44,070 --> 00:09:46,710
Well, if you're so smart, you get the bird out.

215
00:09:46,710 --> 00:09:48,220
No, you're the one who let him in.

216
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:50,040
How do you know it wasn't Leonard?

217
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:52,150
Come on.

218
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:57,280
What about that sweater?

219
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,020
No, it's not good enough.

220
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,090
It has to be perfect.

221
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:03,060
I think the nicest gifts I've got from Howie

222
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:05,170
show how well he knows me.

223
00:10:06,030 --> 00:10:08,830
Let's see, what do I know about Amy?

224
00:10:08,830 --> 00:10:12,820
She loves medieval literature; Chaucer's her favorite.

225
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:16,860
And her eyes sparkle when she watches old French movies.

226
00:10:17,190 --> 00:10:20,930
I enjoy how harp music causes her fingers to dance

227
00:10:20,930 --> 00:10:23,320
as if she's playing along.

228
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:26,510
Wow, you really do love her.

229
00:10:27,510 --> 00:10:29,120
I do.

230
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:31,630
Now, let's find the kind of gift

231
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:34,820
that makes her feel small and worthless.

232
00:11:04,550 --> 00:11:06,110
You won!

233
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:10,320
Certainly doesn't feel like it, does it?

234
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:15,630
You know, my wife used to throw theme parties like this all the time.

235
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:18,350
Oh, I guess that's where Raj gets it from.

236
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:19,990
Well, he and his mother

237
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:21,730
spent a lot of time together when he was young.

238
00:11:21,730 --> 00:11:23,690
I was always working.

239
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:27,600
Hey, you know, Raj is dating a doctor who works a lot.

240
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,740
Him and his mom have a type.

241
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:33,300
You g... Y-You got to laugh at that, right?

242
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,050
No? All right.

243
00:11:38,930 --> 00:11:42,070
All right, let me see if I've got this straight.

244
00:11:42,730 --> 00:11:44,760
A picture of you on my lap

245
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:46,560
is a way to punish your girlfriend

246
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,010
for making you celebrate Christmas?

247
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,250
Correct.

248
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:55,170
Santa thinks dating you may be punishment enough.

249
00:11:57,130 --> 00:11:59,220
There's an argument for that.

250
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:01,240
But I want to make sure.

251
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,310
Smile.

252
00:12:02,310 --> 00:12:04,110
Ho, ho, ho!

253
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:12,000
Okay. On the count of three,

254
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,050
I'll shoot the fire extinguisher and get him airborne.

255
00:12:14,050 --> 00:12:16,350
Howard, you wave the blanket and guide him towards the exit.

256
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:19,150
Raj, you hold open the curtain so he can fly out.

257
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:21,310
Are you sure a dummy like me can handle something

258
00:12:21,310 --> 00:12:23,950
as complicated as a blanket?

259
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:25,800
Do you want the fire extinguisher?

260
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,050
- Yeah, I do. - Great.

261
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:27,920
Here you go.

262
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,120
Okay.

263
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:35,700
One, two, three.

264
00:12:39,070 --> 00:12:40,640
Uh, you have to take the pin out.

265
00:12:44,690 --> 00:12:47,620
You miss the blanket now, don't you?

266
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:50,900
On three.

267
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:53,410
One, two, three.

268
00:13:02,150 --> 00:13:04,390
What did you do?

269
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:05,730
It was an accident.

270
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:07,770
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

271
00:13:07,770 --> 00:13:09,180
Relax, it wasn't your fault.

272
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,880
Uh, maybe it's just stunned.

273
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:13,210
Dude, I-it's not breathing.

274
00:13:13,210 --> 00:13:16,390
Oh, no. I killed it.

275
00:13:16,390 --> 00:13:18,520
Oh, not again.

276
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,730
What do you mean, not again?

277
00:13:23,830 --> 00:13:25,230
When I was ten,

278
00:13:25,230 --> 00:13:27,370
I was playing in my backyard and...

279
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,780
sat on a blue jay.

280
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:36,270
I mean, I tried to bring it back to life with electricity,

281
00:13:36,270 --> 00:13:38,300
but it just...

282
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,400
caught on fire.

283
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:45,900
The worst part was it smelled delicious.

284
00:13:48,010 --> 00:13:49,670
Uh, guys, I found an article here

285
00:13:49,670 --> 00:13:52,040
that says you can do CPR on birds.

286
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:53,570
Great! Do it!

287
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:55,330
I'm not doing it. You killed him, you do it.

288
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:56,840
- I'll do it. - No.

289
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:58,770
I need to do it.

290
00:13:58,770 --> 00:14:00,520
This is on me.

291
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:05,270
Okay.

292
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:09,020
"Mouth over beak and light chest compressions."

293
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:09,910
Don't blow too hard.

294
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:12,470
If you pop him, I will vomit.

295
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,320
Anything?

296
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,710
I am tasting a lot of Slim Jim.

297
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:24,780
Wait, wait, his wing moved!

298
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,560
Oh, he blinked his eyes! He's alive!

299
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,120
It's a Christmas miracle!

300
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:31,440
I might argue a Hanukkah miracle, but I'll take it.

301
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:34,130
Come on, little guy, let's get you outside. Get the curtain.

302
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:44,660
Someone should really close that loading door.

303
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:52,870
Well, that's that.

304
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:54,410
The room's compromised.

305
00:14:54,410 --> 00:14:56,280
They'll have to change all the filters,

306
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:59,040
probably shut it down for weeks.

307
00:14:59,370 --> 00:15:02,200
You were right. Go ahead, call Building Services.

308
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:04,790
- Tell them it was my fault. - No, we're both to blame.

309
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:06,660
You know, let me take the heat on this one.

310
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:07,660
Yeah, just leave me out of it.

311
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:09,150
You know if they come here and see crap everywhere,

312
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:11,590
they're just gonna blame the Indian guy.

313
00:15:16,830 --> 00:15:18,960
Hey. I'm sorry, we're still here.

314
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,150
Is everything okay?

315
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:21,500
It's kind of boring.

316
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,970
Although it did get exciting for a minute

317
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:25,360
when Amy inhaled a wool ball.

318
00:15:26,780 --> 00:15:28,060
How much longer do you think you'll be?

319
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:28,900
I don't know.

320
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,430
There's still a bird in here.

321
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,330
We are gonna get in a ton of trouble.

322
00:15:32,330 --> 00:15:33,550
Honey, it's Christmas Eve.

323
00:15:33,550 --> 00:15:34,590
Who even knows you're in there?

324
00:15:34,590 --> 00:15:36,740
No, our names are on the sign-in sheet.

325
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,490
So erase them and walk out.

326
00:15:38,490 --> 00:15:40,410
I can't do that.

327
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:41,350
Can't do what?

328
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:44,310
She says take our names off the sign-in sheet and leave.

329
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:46,970
- We can't do that. - Yeah.

330
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:52,250
* Jingle bells, jingle bells, jingle all the way *

331
00:15:52,250 --> 00:15:53,980
* Oh, what fun it is to ride *

332
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:56,470
* in a one-horse open sleigh, hey! *

333
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:01,520
Amy, that pudding was delicious.

334
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,890
If you like raisins.

335
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,620
Thank you. And it's figs.

336
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,590
Oh, in that case, it was pretty good.

337
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:13,410
You feeling okay? You hardly touched your goose.

338
00:16:13,410 --> 00:16:16,200
It smelled too much like blue jay.

339
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:18,110
Can I help you clean up?

340
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:19,970
Oh, you Heimliched a ball of wool out of me;

341
00:16:19,970 --> 00:16:21,210
you're good.

342
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:25,200
Uh, what do you say we exchange gifts?

343
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,630
Oh, Sheldon, we didn't bring any.

344
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:28,160
I thought you hate giving gifts.

345
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,050
Yeah, I do.

346
00:16:29,050 --> 00:16:32,620
Which is why I got Amy this.

347
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:34,410
You got me something?

348
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:35,830
Oh, not just something, no.

349
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:38,580
It's from the heart, it's holiday-themed,

350
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:42,910
and I swallowed the gift receipt so you cannot return it.

351
00:16:46,090 --> 00:16:48,620
Look at you on Santa's lap.

352
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,970
That's so sweet.

353
00:16:49,970 --> 00:16:53,090
Of course it is. It's the perfect gift.

354
00:16:53,090 --> 00:16:54,760
H-How are you feeling right now?

355
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:57,340
Guilty? Sad?

356
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:59,160
Wishing you were Jewish?

357
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:02,380
No, I love it.

358
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:03,660
Oh, really?

359
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:05,510
Well, how about now?

360
00:17:06,890 --> 00:17:11,170
Happy holidays to my dear Amy.

361
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:13,470
I hope you treasure this

362
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:16,950
as much as I treasure you.

363
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:20,930
And you got me nothing.

364
00:17:21,530 --> 00:17:23,130
Christmas is ruined.

365
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:25,790
Let's never speak of it again.

366
00:17:25,790 --> 00:17:28,250
Well, this was fun.

367
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:30,320
Actually,

368
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:33,130
I did get you something.

369
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:35,520
But what about our agreement?

370
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:38,480
Well, you got me something. Here.

371
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:44,350
Cookies?

372
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:47,550
They're your Meemaw's Christmas cookies.

373
00:17:47,550 --> 00:17:50,290
I called and got the recipe.

374
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,970
They're perfect.

375
00:18:02,990 --> 00:18:05,110
It tastes like her hugs.

376
00:18:07,730 --> 00:18:10,420
Merry Christmas, Sheldon.

377
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:13,250
I can't believe this.

378
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:17,180
You're happy, I'm happy.

379
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:19,630
Well, maybe a holiday that's all about giving isn't so...

380
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:21,550
Get your hand out of that box!

381
00:18:26,690 --> 00:18:27,740
Okay.

382
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:32,010
The next game is called Hot Boiled Beans.

383
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:35,060
Of course it is.

384
00:18:35,930 --> 00:18:37,910
One person is sent out of the room

385
00:18:37,910 --> 00:18:40,580
while the others hide a small item.

386
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:43,750
Then they invite the first person back by saying,

387
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:45,770
"Hot boiled beans and bacon for supper,

388
00:18:45,770 --> 00:18:48,570
hurry up before it gets cold."

389
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:54,550
If you people think this is better than Tom Hanks-giving,

390
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,620
you're all crazy.

